// ================================================================================================
// ATR-NORMALIZED PHASE MOMENTUM, MULTI-SESSION VWAP FILTER -- a Pine port of the NinjaScript
// strategy ATR_NORMALIZED_PHASE_MOMENTUM_MULTI_SESSION_VWAP_v2 (10-minute decision bars).
//
//     OSCILLATOR  phase = EMA3( 100 * (close - EMA21) / (3 * ATR14) ), every recursion seeded and
//                 smoothed exactly as the source: EMA21 seeded at the first close, ATR14 seeded as
//                 the mean of the first 14 true ranges then Wilder-smoothed, EMA3 seeded at the
//                 first raw value. NOT ta.ema / ta.atr, whose seeds differ.
//     INTENT      phase crosses ABOVE +100 -> long intent; crosses BELOW -100 -> short intent.
//     ADMISSION   a new side is taken only when the completed signal bar's close is strictly less
//                 than 2.5 x ATR14 from the session HLC3-volume VWAP, which accumulates over the
//                 decision bars that OPEN inside the VWAP window and includes the signal bar.
//     WINDOW      the FILL (the next bar's open = this bar's close time) must land inside the entry
//                 window. Outside it an opposite cross exits without reversing. Rejected intents
//                 are neither delayed nor replayed. A rejected reversal still exits the held side.
//     SHADOW      the unfiltered rule keeps its own position ("control shadow"); the filtered
//                 position is that shadow gated by VWAP admission at entry time. A cross to the side
//                 the shadow already holds is a no-op even when the real position is flat.
//     CASH CLOSE  on the bar that closes at the cash close the position is flattened and the shadow
//                 cleared; cash close outranks a simultaneous cross. No stop, target, trail or
//                 pyramiding. One contract.
//     PROFILES    USIndex: entries 09:30-11:00, VWAP 09:30-16:00, cash 16:00, ETH from 18:00.
//                 ComexGold: entries 08:20-09:50, VWAP 08:20-13:30, cash 13:30, ETH from 18:00.
//                 Custom: HHmm inputs, validated as the source validates them. All New York time.
//
// WHAT A PINE PORT CANNOT DO, AND WHAT THIS ONE DOES INSTEAD
//  1. The source builds exact UTC-aligned 10-minute bars from ten contiguous 1-minute components
//     and omits any bucket with a missing minute. A CME 10-minute chart bar on TradingView IS that
//     bucket (sessions open on a ten-minute boundary in every whole-hour zone); TradingView omits
//     minutes that print no trade, so the constituent count is not checked -- the FTM port measured
//     that constraint at zero on 1.05M minutes.
//  2. The source pre-scans loaded history and blocks any session whose 09:20-15:59 minute window is
//     incomplete BEFORE its first bar. Pine cannot look ahead: a session is blocked from the bar a
//     gap is detected (decision-bar level), and the source's frozen 68-date MNQ calendar is applied
//     at session start exactly as the source applies it.
//  3. Every fail-closed path in the source halts the strategy permanently. Here each one is COUNTED,
//     shown on the panel, and by default converted to "flatten, block this session, continue" so a
//     report cannot go silently empty. "Halt on anomaly" restores the source's behaviour.
//  4. The 16:00 cash exit is an order placed at the 15:50 bar's close, filling at the 16:00 bar's
//     open -- the same fill the source gets from a market order after the completed decision bar.
//  5. IsExitOnSessionCloseStrategy (30 s before the session ends) becomes a close at the close of
//     the session's last bar, via session.islastbar.
//  6. The roll-like reset (a >400-tick gap between the 23:59 and 00:00 UTC minutes) is ported as
//     written. On a TradingView continuous contract the roll gap sits at the session open, not at
//     00:00 UTC, so it will rarely fire; use a back-adjusted series or a single contract.
//  7. Costs: slippage 1 tick as the source; commission 0.72 per contract per side (real MNQ stack).
//
// MEASURED (docs/ib/STUDY_APM_VWAP.md; research/apm/). As specified, MNQ costs: NQ 10m research
// n 70, 58.6% win, PF 1.62, +24.0 pts/trade; locked n 34, 67.6%, PF 4.12, +62.8 -- the wrong shape,
// 2022-2024 flatters it on every feed. Beats a random entry with its own exits on NQ research
// (p 0.054), NQ 15m research (0.013), US100 research and validation (0.019, 0.032); FAILS the US100
// test block (p 0.230, 2025 at -27 a trade) and is NULL on US30 over nine years. The DIRECTION call
// is the asset (coin-flip side on the rule's bars: p 0.05 / 0.001); the ENTRY TIMING is a cost -- a
// random bar on the same day with the same side beats the rule everywhere, because the fill has
// already chased 3.97 ATR of a 4.99 ATR day. The VWAP band is also the clock: 0% of crosses after
// 11:00 sit inside it. Walk-forward re-selection loses to these defaults on NQ and US100, so do not
// tune it. Research-block P(mean<=0) 0.052; p99 drawdown about $2,400 per MNQ. One MNQ on $50k
// cannot pass a 6% evaluation; two pass 42-70% and bust 15-24%. VERDICT: not live-ready on this
// evidence -- forward-test with one contract for 40+ trades before sizing.
//
// PROTECTIVE EXITS -- ADDED, NOT IN THE SOURCE, AND MEASURED BEFORE BEING ADDED
// The source has no stop, target, trail or flatten: it exits at the cash close or an opposite
// cross. Three optional exits are added here. The entry set is UNCHANGED by any of them -- entries
// depend on the SHADOW (the unfiltered rule's own position) and never on the real position, and
// reversals never fire on this data -- so they can only change where a trade ends.
// Measured on 8 market-blocks across NQ, US100 and US30 (research/apm/run_p2.py):
//
//   STOP, ships ON at 3.0 x ATR14.  The stop axis is MONOTONE TOWARD WIDER, so every stop costs
//     per-trade edge: $/trade runs 13.99 / 18.31 / 22.61 / 24.27 / 26.35 / 27.84 at 1.0 / 1.5 /
//     2.0 / 2.5 / 3.0 / 6.0 N against $30.93 with NO STOP. Ninth family on this branch with that
//     shape. It ships ON anyway because WITHOUT IT the worst single trade is -$1,271 on US100 and
//     -$1,087 on US30 on a rule earning $11-$35 a trade; at 3.0N those become -$277 and -$536 and
//     the worst FIVE trades fall from -$2,512 to -$904 on US100. At 3.0N Sharpe peaks (0.923 vs
//     0.849), return/drawdown peaks (3.21 vs 2.59), mean drawdown falls $1,166 -> $942, and US30's
//     research block crosses from -$7.87 to +$0.29 a trade. IT IS A RISK TRANSFORMATION, NOT AN
//     IMPROVEMENT -- it buys a bounded tail with about 15% of the per-trade result.
//     AND IT DOES NOT HELP EVERYWHERE. Per block, source -> with the 3.0N stop, $/trade and
//     return-over-drawdown:
//        NQ    research   n  70   $48.03 -> $44.46    r/DD 2.98 -> 3.01
//        NQ    LOCKED     n  34  $125.62 -> $70.73    r/DD 8.78 -> 3.87    <- hurts badly
//        US100 research   n 176   $10.77 -> $13.67    r/DD 2.97 -> 6.01
//        US100 validation n  70   $34.55 -> $42.21    r/DD 5.06 -> 9.04
//        US100 test       n  62   $15.31 -> $28.56    r/DD 0.72 -> 3.10    <- helps most
//        US30  research   n 148   -$7.87 ->  $0.29    r/DD -0.54 -> 0.03
//        US30  validation n  68   $16.41 -> $18.97    r/DD 0.57 -> 0.90
//        US30  test       n  51    $4.58 -> -$8.13    r/DD 0.20 -> -0.25   <- hurts
//     Five of eight blocks improve on $/trade and six of eight on return/drawdown; the two it
//     hurts are NQ's locked block (34 trades) and US30's test block (51 trades). Drawdown falls on
//     seven of eight. If you trade NQ specifically, note that its out-of-sample block is the one
//     the stop damages most -- and that it is 34 trades.
//   TARGET, ships OFF.  No target $26.35 a trade, 6 ATR $23.88, 3 ATR $11.49. The 25th independent
//     time no-take-profit has beaten every target tested here.
//   FLATTEN, ships OFF.  Destructive at every time and monotonically less so the later it is:
//     11:00 $8.24, 12:00 $18.19, 13:00 $17.99, 14:00 $23.81, 15:00 $27.81, 15:30 $29.69 against
//     $30.93 for the cash close. Sixteenth confirmation. If you want one, use 15:30, where it costs
//     ~$1.20 a trade and lifts profit factor 1.70 -> 1.92 and return/drawdown 2.59 -> 3.51.
//
// The bracket is written WITH the entry, in ticks, so it is FILL-RELATIVE and live on the fill bar
// -- `strategy.position_avg_price` is `na` there, so any level derived from it would silently do
// nothing. Its distance uses ATR at the SIGNAL bar, which is knowable when the order is written.
// Set the stop off, the target off and the flatten off to run the source exactly.
//
// CHART: 10-MINUTE, EXTENDED HOURS ON (the session date rolls at 18:00 New York and the VWAP window
// needs the 09:20 bar). Every var write sits under barstate.isconfirmed. Not financial advice.
// ================================================================================================
//@version=6
strategy("ATR phase momentum + session VWAP (NT8 port)", shorttitle = "APM-VWAP", overlay = true,
     pyramiding = 0, calc_on_every_tick = false, process_orders_on_close = false,
     initial_capital = 50000, currency = currency.USD, default_qty_type = strategy.fixed,
     default_qty_value = 1, commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract,
     commission_value = 0.72, slippage = 1)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- inputs
grpP = "Session profile (New York time)"
profileIn = input.string("Automatic", "Profile", options = ["Automatic", "USIndex", "ComexGold",
     "Custom"], group = grpP,
     tooltip = "Automatic resolves ES/MES/NQ/MNQ to USIndex and GC/MGC to ComexGold; any other "
     + "symbol falls back to the USIndex clocks with a panel warning (the source refuses).")
cEntStart = input.int(930, "Custom: entry start (HHmm, inclusive)", minval = 0, maxval = 2359,
     group = grpP)
cEntEnd = input.int(1100, "Custom: entry end (HHmm, exclusive)", minval = 0, maxval = 2359,
     group = grpP)
cVwapStart = input.int(930, "Custom: VWAP start (HHmm, inclusive)", minval = 0, maxval = 2359,
     group = grpP)
cVwapEnd = input.int(1600, "Custom: VWAP end (HHmm, exclusive)", minval = 0, maxval = 2359,
     group = grpP)
cCash = input.int(1600, "Custom: cash close (HHmm)", minval = 0, maxval = 2359, group = grpP)
cEth = input.int(1800, "Custom: electronic session start (HHmm)", minval = 0, maxval = 2359,
     group = grpP)

grpR = "Rule (source constants)"
emaLen = input.int(21, "EMA length", minval = 1, group = grpR)
atrLen = input.int(14, "ATR length (Wilder)", minval = 1, group = grpR)
oscLen = input.int(3, "Oscillator EMA length", minval = 1, group = grpR)
atrDen = input.float(3.0, "ATR denominator multiplier", minval = 0.1, step = 0.5, group = grpR)
upperX = input.float(100.0, "Upper extreme (long intent on a cross above)", step = 10.0,
     group = grpR)
lowerX = input.float(-100.0, "Lower extreme (short intent on a cross below)", step = 10.0,
     group = grpR)
vwapMult = input.float(2.5, "Admit only within x ATR14 of session VWAP", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25,
     group = grpR)

grpT = "Trading"
startDate = input.int(20200203, "Start trading date (yyyyMMdd)", minval = 19000101,
     maxval = 29991231, group = grpT,
     tooltip = "Earlier sessions update state but never submit orders.")
strictTf = input.bool(true, "Require a 10-minute chart (the source's decision bar)", group = grpT)

grpX = "Protective exits -- NOT IN THE SOURCE. Measured before being added; see the tooltips."
useStop = input.bool(true, "ATR stop loss", group = grpX,
     tooltip = "THE SOURCE HAS NO STOP AT ALL, so this is a change to the strategy and it was "
     + "measured before it was added (research/apm/run_p2.py, 8 market-blocks across NQ/US100/US30)."
     + "\n\nWHY IT DEFAULTS ON: without a stop the worst single trade is -$1,271 on US100 and "
     + "-$1,087 on US30, on a rule that earns $11-$35 a trade. At 3.0 ATR those become -$277 and "
     + "-$536, and the worst five trades together fall from -$2,512 to -$904 on US100."
     + "\n\nWHAT IT COSTS: the stop axis is MONOTONE TOWARD WIDER -- averaged over all eight "
     + "blocks, $/trade runs 13.99 at 1.0N, 18.31 at 1.5N, 22.61 at 2.0N, 24.27 at 2.5N, 26.35 at "
     + "3.0N, 27.84 at 6.0N and 30.93 with NO STOP. So any stop costs per-trade edge; 3.0N costs "
     + "about 15% of it."
     + "\n\nWHY 3.0 ANYWAY: Sharpe PEAKS there (0.923 against 0.849 with no stop), "
     + "return/drawdown peaks there (3.21 against 2.59), mean drawdown falls $1,166 -> $942, and "
     + "US30's research block goes from -$7.87 a trade to +$0.29. It is a risk transformation, "
     + "not an improvement. Turn it off to run the source exactly.")
stopAtr = input.float(3.0, "Stop distance, x ATR14 at the signal bar", minval = 0.25, step = 0.25,
     group = grpX,
     tooltip = "Anchored to ATR at the SIGNAL bar, which is knowable when the order is written -- "
     + "the fill price does not exist yet. The bracket goes out WITH the entry so the fill bar is "
     + "protected; a bracket placed one bar later leaves it naked, which is the parity defect "
     + "measured at 4.4-13.0% of trades on this branch.")
useTgt = input.bool(false, "ATR take profit", group = grpX,
     tooltip = "DEFAULT OFF AND IT SHOULD STAY OFF. Averaged over the same eight blocks: no target "
     + "$26.35 a trade, a 6 ATR target $23.88, a 3 ATR target $11.49. That is the 25th independent "
     + "time on this branch that NO TAKE PROFIT has beaten every target tested.")
tgtAtr = input.float(6.0, "Target distance, x ATR14 at the signal bar", minval = 0.5, step = 0.5,
     group = grpX)
useFlat = input.bool(false, "Hard flatten before the cash close", group = grpX,
     tooltip = "DEFAULT OFF. A hard flatten is DESTRUCTIVE at every time tested, and monotonically "
     + "less so the later it is: against the cash-close baseline of $30.93 a trade, 11:00 gives "
     + "$8.24, 12:00 $18.19, 13:00 $17.99, 14:00 $23.81, 15:00 $27.81 and 15:30 $29.69. Sixteenth "
     + "confirmation of that finding here."
     + "\n\nThe one thing it buys: at 15:30 the cost is about $1.20 a trade and profit factor "
     + "rises 1.70 -> 1.92 with return/drawdown 2.59 -> 3.51, because it only moves the exit "
     + "forward by half an hour. If you want one, use a LATE one.")
flatHHmm = input.int(1530, "Flatten at (HHmm, New York)", minval = 0, maxval = 2359, group = grpX)

grpF = "Safety (each gate is counted on the panel)"
resetTicks = input.int(400, "Reset gap threshold at 00:00 UTC (ticks, 0 = off)", minval = 0,
     group = grpF)
postResetBars = input.int(21, "Bars to requalify after a reset", minval = 0, group = grpF)
frozenMode = input.string("Auto (MNQ only)", "Frozen 68-date MNQ incomplete-session calendar",
     options = ["Auto (MNQ only)", "On", "Off"], group = grpF)
haltOnAnomaly = input.bool(false, "Halt permanently on an anomaly (the source's behaviour)",
     group = grpF, tooltip = "Off: flatten, block the rest of that session, count it, continue.")
useBackstop = input.bool(true, "Flatten on the session's last bar (session-close backstop)",
     group = grpF)
showHud = input.bool(true, "Show panel", group = "Display")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- chart and profile resolution
tfMin = timeframe.isminutes ? timeframe.multiplier : 0
if tfMin == 0
    runtime.error("APM-VWAP needs an intraday minute chart (the source specifies 10 minutes).")
if strictTf and tfMin != 10
    runtime.error("The source specifies a 10-minute chart. Turn off 'Require a 10-minute chart' "
         + "to run the port on another minute timeframe.")

hhmm(int v) =>
    int(math.floor(v / 100)) * 60 + v % 100

fmtMin(int m) =>
    h = int(math.floor(m / 60))
    mm = m % 60
    (h < 10 ? "0" : "") + str.tostring(h) + ":" + (mm < 10 ? "0" : "") + str.tostring(mm)

root = syminfo.root
isIdx = root == "ES" or root == "MES" or root == "NQ" or root == "MNQ"
isGold = root == "GC" or root == "MGC"
autoFallback = profileIn == "Automatic" and not isIdx and not isGold
resolved = profileIn == "Automatic" ? (isGold ? "ComexGold" : "USIndex") : profileIn

entStart = resolved == "USIndex" ? 570 : resolved == "ComexGold" ? 500 : hhmm(cEntStart)
entEnd = resolved == "USIndex" ? 660 : resolved == "ComexGold" ? 590 : hhmm(cEntEnd)
vwapStart = resolved == "USIndex" ? 570 : resolved == "ComexGold" ? 500 : hhmm(cVwapStart)
vwapEnd = resolved == "USIndex" ? 960 : resolved == "ComexGold" ? 810 : hhmm(cVwapEnd)
cashClose = resolved == "USIndex" ? 960 : resolved == "ComexGold" ? 810 : hhmm(cCash)
ethStart = resolved == "USIndex" ? 1080 : resolved == "ComexGold" ? 1080 : hhmm(cEth)

// the source's fail-closed configuration checks, verbatim in intent
if entStart < tfMin or entStart >= entEnd or entEnd > cashClose
    runtime.error("Entry window must be ordered and end no later than the cash close.")
if vwapStart >= vwapEnd or vwapEnd > cashClose
    runtime.error("VWAP window must be ordered and end no later than the cash close.")
if cashClose >= ethStart
    runtime.error("Cash close must precede the electronic-session boundary.")
if entStart % tfMin != 0 or entEnd % tfMin != 0 or vwapStart % tfMin != 0
     or vwapEnd % tfMin != 0 or cashClose % tfMin != 0 or ethStart % tfMin != 0
    runtime.error("All session boundaries must align to the decision bar (" + str.tostring(tfMin)
         + " minutes).")
firstQual = math.max(entStart, vwapStart + tfMin)
if firstQual >= entEnd or firstQual > vwapEnd
    runtime.error("Entry and VWAP windows must permit at least one VWAP-qualified fill.")

flatMin = hhmm(flatHHmm)
if useFlat and (flatMin <= entStart or flatMin > cashClose or flatMin % tfMin != 0)
    runtime.error("The hard flatten must sit after the entry window opens, no later than the cash "
         + "close, and align to the decision bar.")

relevantFirst = math.min(vwapStart, entStart - tfMin)   // first decision-bar OPEN that must exist
required = (cashClose - relevantFirst) / tfMin           // decision bars the cash window must hold

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the frozen MNQ calendar
// The source skips these 68 sessions on MNQ because at least one 09:20-15:59 New York minute is
// absent from its frozen minute dataset; it applies only through 2026-08-17.
var int[] frozenCal = array.new<int>()
if barstate.isfirst
    array.concat(frozenCal, array.from(20200120, 20200217, 20200309, 20200312, 20200313, 20200316,
         20200318, 20200525, 20200611, 20200703))
    array.concat(frozenCal, array.from(20200907, 20200910, 20201126, 20201127, 20201224, 20210118,
         20210215, 20210402, 20210531, 20210705))
    array.concat(frozenCal, array.from(20210906, 20211125, 20211126, 20220117, 20220221, 20220530,
         20220620, 20220704, 20220905, 20221124))
    array.concat(frozenCal, array.from(20221125, 20230116, 20230220, 20230407, 20230529, 20230619,
         20230703, 20230704, 20230904, 20231123))
    array.concat(frozenCal, array.from(20231124, 20240115, 20240219, 20240527, 20240619, 20240703,
         20240704, 20240902, 20241128, 20241129))
    array.concat(frozenCal, array.from(20241224, 20250109, 20250120, 20250217, 20250526, 20250619,
         20250703, 20250704, 20250901, 20251127))
    array.concat(frozenCal, array.from(20251128, 20251224, 20260119, 20260216, 20260403, 20260525,
         20260619, 20260703))
useFrozen = frozenMode == "On" or (frozenMode == "Auto (MNQ only)" and root == "MNQ")
frozenEnd = 20260817

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- clocks
tz = "America/New_York"
nyMod = hour(time, tz) * 60 + minute(time, tz)                      // this bar's OPEN minute
nyKey = year(time, tz) * 10000 + month(time, tz) * 100 + dayofmonth(time, tz)
tNext = time + 86400000
nextKey = year(tNext, tz) * 10000 + month(tNext, tz) * 100 + dayofmonth(tNext, tz)
sessKey = nyMod >= ethStart ? nextKey : nyKey                       // the source's SessionDate
closeMod = nyMod + tfMin                                             // fill minute of an order here
inVwapWin = nyMod >= vwapStart and nyMod < vwapEnd
inEntryFill = closeMod >= entStart and closeMod < entEnd
aE = 2.0 / (emaLen + 1.0)
aO = 2.0 / (oscLen + 1.0)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- state
var int curSess = na
var bool sessBlocked = false
var bool cashDone = false
var int expOpen = na
var int reqCount = 0
var bool halted = false
var bool sawEth = false
var float ema = na
var float atr = na
var float prevC = na
var int trN = 0
var float trSum = 0.0
var float osc = na
var bool oscInit = false
var int segBar = 0
var bool postReset = false
var int shadow = 0                     // the unfiltered rule's own position: 1 long, -1 short, 0 flat
var int vwapDay = na
var float cumPV = 0.0
var float cumV = 0.0
var float lastVwap = na
var float lastDist = na
var bool lastAdmit = false
var bool flatDone = false
var float pendAtr = na              // ATR at the signal bar, for the bracket written with the entry
var string pendId = ""
var int nStopExit = 0
var int nTgtExit = 0
var int nFlatExit = 0
// diagnostics, mirroring the source's terminal summary
var int nDecision = 0
var int nBlocked = 0
var int nResets = 0
var int nLong = 0
var int nShort = 0
var int nRev = 0
var int nOppExit = 0
var int nCashExit = 0
var int nAdmit = 0
var int nReject = 0
var int nUnavail = 0
var int nRejectRev = 0
var int nAnom = 0
var string lastAnom = "-"
bool markLong = false
bool markShort = false
bool markReject = false

pos = strategy.position_size > 0 ? 1 : strategy.position_size < 0 ? -1 : 0

// Which protective order closed the last trade, for the panel. A trade that closed since the
// previous bar is inspected by its exit comment; strategy.closedtrades is the reliable trigger
// because a position that opens and stops out inside ONE bar never shows in position_size[1].
var int lastClosed = 0
if barstate.isconfirmed and strategy.closedtrades > lastClosed
    for ci = lastClosed to strategy.closedtrades - 1
        cid = strategy.closedtrades.exit_id(ci)
        if cid == "Lx" or cid == "Sx"
            if strategy.closedtrades.profit(ci) > 0 and useTgt
                nTgtExit += 1
            else
                nStopExit += 1
    lastClosed := strategy.closedtrades

if barstate.isconfirmed and not halted
    if nyMod >= ethStart or nyMod < relevantFirst
        sawEth := true
    // ---- session boundary (the source's BeginSession)
    if na(curSess) or sessKey != curSess
        carried = pos != 0 or shadow != 0
        curSess := sessKey
        sessBlocked := useFrozen and sessKey <= frozenEnd and array.includes(frozenCal, sessKey)
        if sessBlocked
            nBlocked += 1
        cashDone := false
        flatDone := false
        expOpen := relevantFirst
        reqCount := 0
        if carried
            nAnom += 1
            lastAnom := "session carry " + str.tostring(sessKey)
            shadow := 0
            if pos != 0
                strategy.close_all(comment = "carry")
            if haltOnAnomaly
                halted := true
    // ---- cash-window completeness at decision-bar level (the source's TrackRequiredWindow)
    if not sessBlocked and not halted
        if nyMod >= relevantFirst and nyMod < cashClose
            if nyMod != expOpen
                sessBlocked := true
                nBlocked += 1
                nAnom += 1
                lastAnom := "gap " + str.tostring(sessKey) + " expected " + fmtMin(expOpen)
            else
                reqCount += 1
                expOpen += tfMin
        else if nyMod >= cashClose and nyMod < ethStart and reqCount != required
            sessBlocked := true
            nBlocked += 1
            nAnom += 1
            lastAnom := "short window " + str.tostring(sessKey) + " " + str.tostring(reqCount)
                 + "/" + str.tostring(required)
        if sessBlocked
            shadow := 0
            if pos != 0
                strategy.close_all(comment = "data gap")
            if haltOnAnomaly
                halted := true
    // ---- a non-blocked decision bar
    if not sessBlocked and not halted
        // roll-like reset: contiguous bars, the 00:00 UTC open, a gap above the threshold
        contiguous = time - time[1] == tfMin * 60000
        utcMidnight = hour(time, "UTC") == 0 and minute(time, "UTC") == 0
        if resetTicks > 0 and contiguous and utcMidnight and not na(close[1])
             and math.abs(open - close[1]) > resetTicks * syminfo.mintick
            if pos != 0 or shadow != 0
                nAnom += 1
                lastAnom := "reset with exposure " + str.tostring(sessKey)
                if pos != 0
                    strategy.close_all(comment = "reset")
                if haltOnAnomaly
                    halted := true
            ema := na
            atr := na
            prevC := na
            trN := 0
            trSum := 0.0
            osc := na
            oscInit := false
            segBar := 0
            postReset := true
            shadow := 0
            vwapDay := na
            cumPV := 0.0
            cumV := 0.0
            nResets += 1
        // the indicator, fed by EVERY decision bar of a non-blocked session, after the cash close too
        oscPrev = osc
        oscPrevAvail = oscInit
        ema := na(ema) ? close : aE * close + (1.0 - aE) * ema
        trng = na(prevC) ? high - low : math.max(high - low, math.abs(high - prevC),
             math.abs(low - prevC))
        prevC := close
        if na(atr)
            trN += 1
            trSum += trng
            if trN == atrLen
                atr := trSum / atrLen
        else
            atr := ((atrLen - 1.0) * atr + trng) / atrLen
        bool oscAvail = false
        if not na(atr) and atr > 0
            raw = 100.0 * (close - ema) / (atrDen * atr)
            osc := oscInit ? aO * raw + (1.0 - aO) * osc : raw
            oscInit := true
            oscAvail := true
        // the session HLC3-volume VWAP over decision bars OPENING inside the window, this bar included
        bool vwapAvail = false
        bool admitted = false
        lastVwap := na
        lastDist := na
        if inVwapWin
            if na(vwapDay) or vwapDay != nyKey
                vwapDay := nyKey
                cumPV := 0.0
                cumV := 0.0
            cumPV += hlc3 * nz(volume)
            cumV += nz(volume)
            if cumV > 0 and not na(atr) and atr > 0
                vwapAvail := true
                lastVwap := cumPV / cumV
                lastDist := math.abs(close - lastVwap) / atr
                admitted := math.abs(close - lastVwap) < vwapMult * atr
        lastAdmit := admitted
        segBar += 1
        nDecision += 1
        // cash close outranks a simultaneous cross; after it, no decision until the next session
        if closeMod == cashClose
            shadow := 0
            if not cashDone
                cashDone := true
                if pos != 0
                    nCashExit += 1
                    strategy.close_all(comment = "cash close")
        else if not cashDone and sessKey >= startDate and oscPrevAvail and oscAvail
             and not (postReset and segBar < postResetBars)
            longX = oscPrev <= upperX and osc > upperX
            shortX = oscPrev >= lowerX and osc < lowerX
            if longX or shortX
                side = longX ? 1 : -1
                prior = shadow
                if prior != side
                    if prior == 0
                        // flat shadow: only a fill inside the entry window can open it
                        if inEntryFill
                            shadow := side
                            if admitted
                                nAdmit += 1
                                pendAtr := atr
                                if side == 1
                                    nLong += 1
                                    markLong := true
                                    pendId := "L"
                                    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, comment = "L")
                                else
                                    nShort += 1
                                    markShort := true
                                    pendId := "S"
                                    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, comment = "S")
                            else
                                nReject += 1
                                markReject := true
                                if not vwapAvail
                                    nUnavail += 1
                    else if not inEntryFill
                        // opposite cross outside the window: the shadow flattens, the held side exits
                        shadow := 0
                        if pos == prior
                            nOppExit += 1
                            strategy.close_all(comment = "opposite cross")
                    else
                        shadow := side
                        if admitted
                            nAdmit += 1
                            if pos == prior
                                nRev += 1
                            pendAtr := atr
                            if side == 1
                                nLong += 1
                                markLong := true
                                pendId := "L"
                                strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, comment = "L")
                            else
                                nShort += 1
                                markShort := true
                                pendId := "S"
                                strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, comment = "S")
                        else
                            nReject += 1
                            nRejectRev += 1
                            markReject := true
                            if not vwapAvail
                                nUnavail += 1
                            if pos == prior
                                nOppExit += 1
                                strategy.close_all(comment = "opposite cross")
    // ---- the protective bracket, written WITH the entry so the fill bar is covered
    // `loss` and `profit` are in TICKS and are FILL-RELATIVE, which is what lets them be placed on
    // the signal bar: strategy.position_avg_price does not exist until one bar after the fill, so
    // any level derived from it is `na` here and silently does nothing (STUDY_SCALP89). The
    // distance uses ATR at the SIGNAL bar, which is knowable when the order is written.
    if (useStop or useTgt) and pendId != "" and not na(pendAtr) and pendAtr > 0
        sTicks = math.max(1, int(math.round(stopAtr * pendAtr / syminfo.mintick)))
        tTicks = math.max(1, int(math.round(tgtAtr * pendAtr / syminfo.mintick)))
        strategy.exit(pendId + "x", from_entry = pendId,
             loss = useStop ? sTicks : na, profit = useTgt ? tTicks : na)
    pendId := ""

    // ---- the hard flatten: an order at this bar's close fills at the next bar's open, so it is
    // submitted on the bar BEFORE the cutoff -- the same convention the cash close already uses.
    if useFlat and not flatDone and not sessBlocked and closeMod >= flatMin and closeMod < cashClose
        flatDone := true
        if pos != 0
            nFlatExit += 1
            strategy.close_all(comment = "flatten " + fmtMin(flatMin))

    // ---- the session-close backstop (the source's IsExitOnSessionCloseStrategy, 30 s early)
    if useBackstop and session.islastbar and pos != 0
        shadow := 0
        strategy.close_all(comment = "session end", immediately = true)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- display
plot(lastVwap, "Session VWAP", color = color.new(color.orange, 0), linewidth = 2,
     style = plot.style_linebr)
bandHi = plot(not na(lastVwap) and not na(atr) ? lastVwap + vwapMult * atr : na, "Admission +",
     color = color.new(color.orange, 70), style = plot.style_linebr)
bandLo = plot(not na(lastVwap) and not na(atr) ? lastVwap - vwapMult * atr : na, "Admission -",
     color = color.new(color.orange, 70), style = plot.style_linebr)
fill(bandHi, bandLo, color = color.new(color.orange, 92), title = "Admission band")
plot(ema, "EMA", color = color.new(color.teal, 40))
plot(osc, "Phase oscillator", display = display.data_window + display.status_line)
plotshape(markLong, "Long intent admitted", style = shape.triangleup, location = location.belowbar,
     color = color.new(color.green, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(markShort, "Short intent admitted", style = shape.triangledown,
     location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(color.red, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(markReject, "Intent rejected by VWAP", style = shape.xcross, location = location.abovebar,
     color = color.new(color.gray, 0), size = size.tiny)
bgcolor(inEntryFill ? color.new(color.blue, 96) : na)
bgcolor(sessBlocked ? color.new(color.red, 94) : na)

var table hud = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 22, border_width = 1)
if showHud and barstate.islast
    sz = size.small
    table.cell(hud, 0, 0, "Profile", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 0, resolved + (autoFallback ? " (fallback for " + root + ")" : ""),
         text_size = sz, text_color = autoFallback ? color.orange : color.gray)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 1, "Entry fills / VWAP / cash", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 1, fmtMin(entStart) + "-" + fmtMin(entEnd) + " / " + fmtMin(vwapStart) + "-"
         + fmtMin(vwapEnd) + " / " + fmtMin(cashClose), text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 2, "Chart", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 2, timeframe.period + "m" + (tfMin == 10 ? "" : " (source: 10m)")
         + (sawEth ? "" : "  NO ETH BARS SEEN"), text_size = sz,
         text_color = tfMin == 10 and sawEth ? color.gray : color.orange)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 3, "Phase oscillator", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 3, na(osc) ? "-" : str.tostring(osc, "#.#"), text_size = sz,
         text_color = na(osc) ? color.gray : osc > upperX ? color.green : osc < lowerX ? color.red
         : color.gray)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 4, "VWAP distance (ATR)", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 4, na(lastDist) ? "outside window" : str.tostring(lastDist, "#.##")
         + (lastAdmit ? " admit" : " reject"), text_size = sz,
         text_color = na(lastDist) ? color.gray : lastAdmit ? color.green : color.red)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 5, "Shadow / position", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 5, (shadow > 0 ? "long" : shadow < 0 ? "short" : "flat") + " / "
         + (pos > 0 ? "long" : pos < 0 ? "short" : "flat"), text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 6, "Decision bars", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 6, str.tostring(nDecision), text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 7, "Blocked sessions", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 7, str.tostring(nBlocked), text_size = sz,
         text_color = nBlocked > 0 ? color.orange : color.gray)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 8, "Resets", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 8, str.tostring(nResets), text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 9, "VWAP admitted / rejected", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 9, str.tostring(nAdmit) + " / " + str.tostring(nReject) + " (unavailable "
         + str.tostring(nUnavail) + ", reversals " + str.tostring(nRejectRev) + ")", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 10, "Long / short entries", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 10, str.tostring(nLong) + " / " + str.tostring(nShort), text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 11, "Reversals", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 11, str.tostring(nRev), text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 12, "Opposite-cross exits", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 12, str.tostring(nOppExit), text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 13, "Cash-close exits", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 13, str.tostring(nCashExit), text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 14, "Anomalies (last)", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 14, str.tostring(nAnom) + " (" + lastAnom + ")", text_size = sz,
         text_color = nAnom > 0 ? color.orange : color.gray)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 15, "Halted", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 15, halted ? "YES -- nothing trades from here" : "no", text_size = sz,
         text_color = halted ? color.red : color.gray)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 16, "Frozen MNQ calendar", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 16, useFrozen ? "applied" : "off", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 17, "First VWAP-qualified fill", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 17, fmtMin(firstQual), text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 18, "Closed trades", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 18, str.tostring(strategy.closedtrades), text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 19, "Protective exits", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 19, (useStop ? "stop " + str.tostring(stopAtr, "#.##") + "N" : "no stop")
         + (useTgt ? " / target " + str.tostring(tgtAtr, "#.##") + "N" : " / no target")
         + (useFlat ? " / flat " + fmtMin(flatMin) : " / no flatten"), text_size = sz,
         text_color = useStop ? color.gray : color.orange)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 20, "Stop / target / flatten hits", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 20, str.tostring(nStopExit) + " / " + str.tostring(nTgtExit) + " / "
         + str.tostring(nFlatExit), text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 21, "Current stop distance", text_size = sz)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 21, not useStop ? "off" : na(atr) ? "-"
         : str.tostring(stopAtr * atr, "#.##") + " pts", text_size = sz)
